§ `Fixtures -- statutory declarations`

`Daniel's client declares before him in his office (d034)` MEANS `Statutory declaration` WITH
    `it is in the Schedule 1 form` IS TRUE
    `the witness is an authorised witness` IS TRUE
    `I signed or personally marked it` IS TRUE
    `I signed or initialled every alteration` IS TRUE
    `I declared the s 12(3)(c) matters orally in the witness's presence` IS TRUE
    `the witness then signed or personally marked it` IS TRUE
    `the witness signed or initialled my alterations` IS TRUE
    `the witness wrote their name and qualification` IS TRUE
    `any departure is saved by s 16` IS FALSE

`the witness forgot their name and qualification` MEANS `Statutory declaration` WITH
    `it is in the Schedule 1 form` IS TRUE
    `the witness is an authorised witness` IS TRUE
    `I signed or personally marked it` IS TRUE
    `I signed or initialled every alteration` IS TRUE
    `I declared the s 12(3)(c) matters orally in the witness's presence` IS TRUE
    `the witness then signed or personally marked it` IS TRUE
    `the witness signed or initialled my alterations` IS TRUE
    `the witness wrote their name and qualification` IS FALSE
    `any departure is saved by s 16` IS FALSE

`the witness forgot their qualification, saved by s 16` MEANS `Statutory declaration` WITH
    `it is in the Schedule 1 form` IS TRUE
    `the witness is an authorised witness` IS TRUE
    `I signed or personally marked it` IS TRUE
    `I signed or initialled every alteration` IS TRUE
    `I declared the s 12(3)(c) matters orally in the witness's presence` IS TRUE
    `the witness then signed or personally marked it` IS TRUE
    `the witness signed or initialled my alterations` IS TRUE
    `the witness wrote their name and qualification` IS FALSE
    `any departure is saved by s 16` IS TRUE

`signed at home and posted to the witness, no oral declaration` MEANS `Statutory declaration` WITH
    `it is in the Schedule 1 form` IS TRUE
    `the witness is an authorised witness` IS TRUE
    `I signed or personally marked it` IS TRUE
    `I signed or initialled every alteration` IS TRUE
    `I declared the s 12(3)(c) matters orally in the witness's presence` IS FALSE
    `the witness then signed or personally marked it` IS TRUE
    `the witness signed or initialled my alterations` IS TRUE
    `the witness wrote their name and qualification` IS TRUE
    `any departure is saved by s 16` IS FALSE

§ `ss 5, 11 -- affirming; declaring about anything`

#ASSERT `May I affirm instead of swearing`
#ASSERT `May I make a statutory declaration about any matter`

§ `Interpretation Act s 5, s 8 -- lawyers and experienced legal practitioners`

-- d034: Daniel is a lawyer by admission; the practising certificate is not what makes him one.
#ASSERT `Am I a lawyer` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a lawyer` TRUE FALSE

-- d034: five years since admission (assumed continuous certificate).
#ASSERT `Am I an experienced legal practitioner` TRUE TRUE 5
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an experienced legal practitioner` TRUE TRUE 1
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an experienced legal practitioner` TRUE FALSE 5

§ `s 12(6), Schedule 2 -- who may witness my statutory declaration`

-- d034: the first three are Daniel. Schedule 2 reaches only declarations made in WA.
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `Daniel, a lawyer, witnesses a client's declaration in Perth (d034)` EQUALS `authorised: a person described in Schedule 2 (s 12(6)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `Daniel witnesses in Melbourne, a Commonwealth witness (assumed)` EQUALS `authorised: a Commonwealth statutory declaration witness (s 12(6)(a)(ii) or (b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `Daniel witnesses in Melbourne, no Commonwealth or Victorian authority` EQUALS `not an authorised witness for a declaration made at that place`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `a nurse witnesses in Bunbury` EQUALS `authorised: a person described in Schedule 2 (s 12(6)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `an NCO with 3 years' service witnesses in Perth` EQUALS `not an authorised witness for a declaration made at that place`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `a neighbour with no listed occupation witnesses in Perth` EQUALS `not an authorised witness for a declaration made at that place`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `an Australian consul witnesses in Bali` EQUALS `authorised: a prescribed consular official working there (s 12(6)(c)(i))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `a London notary public witnesses` EQUALS `authorised: a justice or notary public of that place (s 12(6)(c)(ii))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this statutory declaration` `Daniel witnesses on holiday in Italy, with no local authority` EQUALS `not an authorised witness for a declaration made at that place`

§ `ss 8, 9(6)-(8), 10(5) -- who may witness my affidavit`

-- d034: the first two are Daniel; the third is Daniel in 2021, after d031.
#ASSERT `May I witness this affidavit` `Daniel witnesses an affidavit in Perth for another firm's client (d034)` EQUALS `authorised: an experienced legal practitioner (s 9(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this affidavit` `Daniel witnesses an affidavit he helped prepare (d034)` EQUALS `not authorised: an experienced legal practitioner who took part in preparing it or in its proceedings (s 9(7))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this affidavit` `Daniel in 2021, one year after admission (d031)` EQUALS `not authorised: not yet a legal practitioner for 2 years (s 8)`
#ASSERT `May I witness this affidavit` `a JP who helped prepare the affidavit` EQUALS `authorised: a Justice of the Peace (s 9(6)(a))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this affidavit` `a lawyer admitted 5 years without a practising certificate` EQUALS `not an authorised witness for this affidavit`
#ASSERT `May I witness this affidavit` `a court associate appointed a court authorised witness` EQUALS `authorised: a court authorised witness, for use in that court (s 10(5))`
#ASSERT `May I witness this affidavit` `Daniel witnesses an affidavit in Singapore` EQUALS `not an authorised witness for this affidavit`

§ `ss 12, 16 -- is my statutory declaration validly made`

#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration validly made` `Daniel's client declares before him in his office (d034)` EQUALS `validly made under s 12`
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration validly made` `the witness forgot their name and qualification` EQUALS `not validly made: the witness did not write their name and qualification`
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration validly made` `the witness forgot their qualification, saved by s 16` EQUALS `valid despite a departure: s 16 saves it`
#ASSERT `Is my statutory declaration validly made` `signed at home and posted to the witness, no oral declaration` EQUALS `not validly made: I did not declare orally in the witness's presence`

§ `ss 7(3), 9(3)(c), 12(3)(c) -- remote and electronic`

-- d034: Daniel asked to witness by video link.
#ASSERT `Does the Act let me do it remotely` `swearing an oath or making an affirmation` EQUALS `yes: s 7(3) lets the oath or affirmation be taken by audio or video link`
#ASSERT `Does the Act let me do it remotely` `swearing or affirming an affidavit` EQUALS `not settled by this Act: s 9(3)(c) needs the witness's presence, and s 7(3) may or may not reach the affidavit oath`
#ASSERT `Does the Act let me do it remotely` `making a statutory declaration` EQUALS `not settled by this Act: s 12(3)(c) needs the witness's presence, and no provision speaks of a link for a declaration`
#ASSERT `Does the Act let me do it remotely` `signing my statutory declaration or affidavit electronically` EQUALS `not settled by this Act: it says nothing about electronic signatures`

§ `s 13 -- a blind or illiterate maker`

#ASSERT `Must I read it aloud and certify` TRUE

§ `ss 14, 15 -- will a court accept it`

#ASSERT `Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting it` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not admissible: signed with a rubber stamp (s 15(3))`
#ASSERT `Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting it` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not admissible: no English translation with a translator's affidavit (s 14)`
#ASSERT `Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting it` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ss 14 and 15 do not stand in the way`

§ `s 17 -- pretending to be an authorised witness`

#ASSERT `Do I commit the pretending offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Do I commit the pretending offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for pretending in months` EQUALS 12

§ `Criminal Code s 169 -- a false statement`

#ASSERT `Do I commit the false statement crime` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Do I commit the false statement crime` TRUE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT (`What is the most I face for a false statement` `my statutory declaration`)'s `years of imprisonment on indictment` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT (`What is the most I face for a false statement` `my statutory declaration`)'s `dollars of fine on summary conviction` EQUALS 24000
#ASSERT (`What is the most I face for a false statement` `my affidavit, sworn or affirmed`)'s `years of imprisonment on indictment` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT (`What is the most I face for a false statement` `my affidavit, sworn or affirmed`)'s `years of imprisonment on summary conviction` EQUALS 3
